| H-09 | Release/migrations | Database migration runs in the application startup command. Multiple starting instances can contend, and application availability is coupled to migration execution. | Use one controlled pre-deploy/release migration job with locking, backward-compatible migrations, health gates, and a rollback/runbook strategy. | M |
| H-10 | Delivery safeguards | No active repository CI workflow was found to enforce backend tests, frontend tests/build, migrations, drift, secret scanning, or diff checks before merge. | Add protected-branch CI with deterministic dependency installation, PostgreSQL migration tests, test/build gates, dependency and secret scans, and artifact provenance. | M |
